 appearances, and the color system."}],"url":"\/documentation\/tuikit\/appearanceandcolors","title":"Appearance and Colors"},"doc://TUIkit/documentation/TUIkit/LayoutSystem":{"role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/tuikit\/layoutsystem","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/LayoutSystem","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Understand the two-pass layout used by stacks and other layout containers."}],"kind":"article","title":"Layout System"},"doc://TUIkit/documentation/TUIkit":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/tuikit","identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A declarative, SwiftUI-like framework for building Terminal User Interfaces in Swift."}],"images":[{"identifier":"tuikit-logo.png","type":"icon"},{"identifier":"tuikit-logo.png","type":"card"}],"role":"collection","title":"TUIkit","kind":"symbol"},"doc://TUIkit/documentation/TUIkit/CustomViews":{"type":"topic","kind":"article","title":"Custom Views","url":"\/documentation\/tuikit\/customviews","role":"collectionGroup","identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/CustomViews","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Build your own views by composing existing ones or creating custom view modifiers."}]},"doc://TUIkit/documentation/TUIkit/KeyboardShortcuts":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/KeyboardShortcuts","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"How keyboard input flows through TUIkit: from raw terminal bytes to your view handlers."}],"role":"collectionGroup","title":"Keyboard Shortcuts","url":"\/documentation\/tuikit\/keyboardshortcuts","type":"topic"},"tuikit-logo.png":{"identifier":"tuikit-logo.png","variants":[{"traits":["1x","light"],"url":"\/images\/TUIkit\/tuikit-logo.png"}],"alt":"TUIkit Logo","type":"image"},"doc://TUIkit/documentation/TUIkit/ListAndTable":{"url":"\/documentation\/tuikit\/listandtable","type":"topic","role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/List